<!-- ABOUT CONTENT -->
<section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What is SwiftCart?</h2>

    <p>
        SwiftCart is a lightweight academic e-commerce web application developed
        to demonstrate core Java web technologies and clean architectural
        practices. It focuses on understanding how real-world applications are
        structured rather than on commercial features.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="section light-bg">
    <h2 class="section-title">Technology Stack</h2>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> JSP, HTML, CSS</li>
        <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Java Servlets</li>
        <li><strong>Database:</strong> MySQL (JDBC)</li>
        <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> MVC + DAO Pattern</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Learning Objectives</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Understand MVC architecture in Java web applications</li>
        <li>Learn DAO pattern with JDBC</li>
        <li>Practice JSP–Servlet interaction</li>
        <li>Build clean, maintainable academic projects</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section light-bg">
    <h2 class="section-title">Disclaimer</h2>

    <p>
        SwiftCart is strictly an academic project. No real products are sold,
        no payments are processed, and no commercial activity is involved.
        All data is used for learning and demonstration purposes only.
    </p>
</section>

<!-- FOOTER -->
<footer class="footer">
